# HD regression (1024): the Dwarf start (hd-dwarf-1024.script) with the loading screen captured, then three clicks at fixed offsets from the screen centre (+200,0 / 0,+150 / -200,-100). Each click target is settled before the capture, so the 1024 and 1366 captures must show the same world (tests/menu/hd_compare.py with the probes 180,230,200,150 460,140,70,60 880,330,120,200 560,70,60,60, away from the animated hero). Held-button walking is time based and not frame deterministic; it shares the click's screen-to-world target code.
